35,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,The bay is capped at four hundred kilos per square metre.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The maintenance log shows seventeen call-outs last season, four during opening hours.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Rin,,"The lab is down to one person, with two hundred pieces waiting.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Kenji,,Two of the last four openings slipped because paperwork arrived after the shipping cut-off.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,Transport and crating ate nearly a third of installation costs.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""name_label"",""name"":""Benjamin"",""self"":true,""raw"":""Benjamin: Transport and crating ate nearly a third of installation costs.""}]}"
40,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Benjamin, does that third of the budget include the shoring we needed for the heavy stonework?","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Daisuke, the shoring was a separate line item, but it confirms your structural worry.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Kenji, if paperwork slips, does the lab’s backlog get worse because we rush the incoming objects?","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, yes, the rush work piles onto the backlog.","{""words"":9,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Toshio, those opening-hours call-outs mean we’re paying for downtime we didn’t budget for.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"@Toshio, so the bay’s limit and the powered displays’ failures both point to the same risk.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Daisuke, precisely. The building’s limits and the equipment’s fragility are the same problem wearing different faces.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Rin,,"@Benjamin, if transport costs are that high, does that mean we should avoid exhibitions needing heavy loans?","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, not necessarily. The slips came from distant lenders. Local items avoid the paperwork risk and the transport costs.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, exactly. Local items also skip the bespoke mount-making fees, which have risen sharply.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"@Toshio, so we need a candidate that respects the bay’s weight limit and avoids powered displays entirely.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"@Daisuke, agreed. We must prioritize candidates that fit the structural limits and require minimal powered maintenance.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Rin,,"@Kenji, if local items are safer, does that mean we can actually staff the room without burning out the one person left in the lab?","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, yes. Local items mean less incoming conservation work, so the single lab staff member can focus on maintenance rather than triage.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Rin, and with local items, we avoid the transport and mount-making costs that quietly swallow the budget.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
