60,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,The candidates are here. I’m looking for one that fits the bay’s weight limit and avoids powered displays.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Toshio,,I’m checking which candidates actually respect the structural limits and avoid the maintenance traps we just identified.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Rin,,"I’m checking who would actually stand in the room, given the lab is down to one person and the volunteer roster is mostly town history guides.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"I’m checking which candidates avoid distant lenders and heavy shipping, so we don’t repeat those opening slips.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,I’m checking which candidates keep the transport and mount-making costs from quietly swallowing the budget.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Toshio, Candidate D’s overhead rigging and dark zones seem to ignore the bay’s weight cap entirely.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Daisuke, agreed. The rigging alone would breach the structural survey’s limits before a single artwork is hung.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Kenji, Candidate A’s demonstration sessions need people present. Can the town history circle actually do that, or is it just walking tours?","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, the circle guides walks, not weaving. We’d need new volunteers or staff, which we don’t have.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Rin, Candidate A’s local focus saves us the transport and mount-making fees, but the staffing gap is real.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,"@Toshio, Candidate C’s visible conservation bench is static, but does the working setup add weight to the walkway?","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Daisuke, the bench is static, but the reconstructions and stonework likely exceed the bay’s cap. It’s a structural risk.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Rin,,"@Kenji, if the circle can’t weave, who stands in the room for Candidate A? We can’t hire new staff.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, the craftspeople themselves perform the demonstrations. We don't need staff to do the work, just to manage the schedule.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, that’s clever, but managing a schedule still requires someone. With the lab at one person, who is left to coordinate the craftspeople?","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,"@Toshio, so C is out due to weight, D is out due to rigging. That leaves A and B.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Toshio,,"@Daisuke, B relies on partner loans, which triggers the transport costs and paperwork risks we just ruled out.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Rin,,"@Kenji, so A is the only one left. But if the craftspeople do the work, who actually stands in the room when they aren’t there?","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, the town history circle can handle the quiet hours. They’re already in the building, so it’s just a shift in duties.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Rin, the circle covers the quiet hours, and the local sourcing keeps the budget intact. I’m voting for A.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
